WEBVTT

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.110
You know,

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.010
I just don't get what Funasaka-san's saying.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.450
Does he really have to get mad, 
just because I put my underwear

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.140
on top of that weird fish-animal?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.720
I figured it would be rude to put 
them on the desk or the chair!

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.750
It's...

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.750
It's?

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.350
A giant monster...

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.500
That's a hologram... Right?

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.770
If it were real, everyone would be screaming.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.970
Is it an ad for something?

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.400
The way it just moved...

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.010
Uh, what is that an ad for?

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.130
You're an idiot sometimes, 
aren't you, Kuroki-kun?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.090
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.720
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.440
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.780
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.100
<b>File 6: Rudra Strikes Back</b>

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.360
<i>I'm in front of the old Shinjuku city hall, 
where an explosion occurred yesterday.</i>

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.660
<i>Police say what happened last night was 
a combination of audio equipment,</i>

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:03.120
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.210
<i>several dozen 3-D projectors, 
as well as explosive devices.</i>

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.970
<i>No one's claimed credit, 
and the goal is unknown.</i>

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.360
<i>The old city hall was already being dismantled,</i>

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.830
It's amazing, no matter how 
many times I see it.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.520
Giant monsters are one of Japan's 
biggest contributions

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.080
<i>so miraculously, no one was injured.</i>

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.620
to world culture.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.090
You're very knowledgeable, Emilia-chan.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.870
All right, goodbye.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.250
Boss,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.020
the Shinjuku PS is requesting 
aid for its investigation.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:27.510
Witnesses report that a Willwear 
assembled the projectors.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:28.720
All right.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.640
After something this big, we need 
to arrest the responsible parties!

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.520
No, that's impossible.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.070
The crime's prime suspect is already dead, 
according to the Shinjuku PS.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.920
They know who it was?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.110
So it seems.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.280
Is the man behind it—

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.520
Huh? Was today trash day?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.470
No. Funasaka-san...

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.160
Yes?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.010
Was the prime suspect

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.150
the movie director Kadoyama Hiromitsu?

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.470
Oh? How did you know?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.250
The Kadoyama Growl.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.210
Kadoyama Growl?

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:05.050
When the monster roared, it moved 
in a very unique way, right?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.910
Oh, you mean this?

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.730
These motions are something

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.600
Director Kadoyama incorporated from kabuki.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.440
Are you a giant monster fan?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.980
I don't know much about them.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.190
I just know a bit about Director Kadoyama.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.250
That's right...

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.960
Hiromitsu Kadoyama was the last 
maestro of giant monster movies

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.080
of the Heisei period.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.330
I am certain

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.940
that Director Kadoyama created that hologram.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.420
But his being behind this must be some mistake.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.660
But the police were sent production 
notes by Director Kadoyama

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.370
that could be interpreted as a claim of credit.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.230
The delivery date was set in advance.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.470
So he shipped them before he died?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.350
What did the notes say?

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.740
"Rudra, the giant monster, will burn 
the land of my revenge to ash."

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.720
That's pretty nuts.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.940
No, it must be some mistake!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.510
But he was arrested before his death.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.910
Chief, may I get permission to 
cooperate with the investigation?

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.810
As a civilian?

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.810
What do we do in these cases, again?

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.710
The law's been changed, so it's no problem.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.030
That's right.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.250
If we want to be sure, 
we should also send Emilia-chan.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.810
We'll say it's part of her training.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.420
<b>Kadoyama</b>

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.820
Kadoyama-san lived alone and had no relatives.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.510
We just started the paperwork to turn 
this house over to the government.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.220
He wasn't the kind of guy to...

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.930
No, that's what we're looking into.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:39.920
Was there anything different

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.900
or strange about him?

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.830
Let me see...

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.610
Sena-san, I found a work contract.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:48.500
He was very active just before his death.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:50.230
It's for a New Zealand CG studio.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.520
I can't say much about his 
activities outside, though...

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.700
And then a German...

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.040
3-D projection mapping?

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.680
What do you mean by "outside"?

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.700
He paid for the whole amount himself

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.320
Well, his work, I suppose.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:59.040
He was away from the house all the time.

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.040
to make several minutes of footage.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:03.880
He didn't seem to me like the kind 
of guy that people would dislike...

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.880
<b>Project R</b>

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.540
Project R?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:09.780
Still, this house has quite an old-fashioned 
design... Or maybe I should say "retro."

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:05.840
Looks like a scenario document.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:10.860
Yes...

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.310
<b>Great Monster 

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.950
"Great Monster Rudra."

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.730
Before his death,

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:21.570
Director Kadoyama was dealing with  
former Minister of Economics Mouri Takerou.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.500
He wanted him to fund a movie project.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.070
Come to think of it,

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:29.280
the Economics Ministry just 
started a support program...

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:37.500
<b>Kadoyama Hiromitsu</b>

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.480
It was a typical government 
project in the same vein

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.660
as the Cool Japan program decades 
ago, which sought to make

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.500
Japan's "coolness" known overseas.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:42.760
But many individuals and companies 
applied, and no one was approved.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.850
The only one awarded funding was

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.510
a projection-mapping project 
to support restorations,

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.610
run by a company associated
with Minister Mouri.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.690
The project they tried after Orochi was fixed?

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.790
I heard that didn't go so well.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.230
It seems that two-thirds of the money 
went back into his pockets.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.940
That happens a lot, but it's still horrible.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:14.160
<b>Kadoyama Hiromitsu</b>

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.660
A year before his death, Kadoyama-san

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.990
was told that he had six months to live.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.890
He planned for this to be his 
last, and greatest, work.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.160
But Minister Mouri's treatment 
of him was terrible.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.990
<b>Minister of Economics and Industry</b>

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:16.990
At least read it.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.760
It's a giant monster movie, but not 
like any that have been made before.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:21.960
It's a new—

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.380
I told you already,

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.170
we can't trust a freelancer.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.960
Make your request through this company.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.700
Please, Mouri-san...

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.220
You yelled at the company I introduced you to.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:39.460
But they wanted sixty percent of the budget

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:41.520
for their own profit. That's crazy.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.220
It's not crazy!

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.110
Every company wants to make a profit.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.590
You're not taking that budget for yourself—

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:50.830
Leave! You're wasting my time!

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:55.090
Mouri-san, what's wrong with it?

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.160
I got a trustworthy company to support me.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.450
I will decide whether

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.940
it's trustworthy or not, fool.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.000
That's the problem with people into sci-fi and—

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.260
What did you say, you ass?!

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:07.420
Got a problem, old man?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.120
Arrest him! Arrest him!

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.030
Stop!

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:10.940
Let me go!

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.960
Mouri!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.110
In the end, not only was his request denied,

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:22.600
but the basic idea was stolen and used 
for a restoration-support event.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.060
So it was ripped off?!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:31.030
<b>Project R</b>

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.510
The idea was.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.320
The actual event was garbage.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.030
He said in his diary that it made him angry.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.870
Was that his motive?

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.610
Revenge on Tokyo for stealing his work?

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.580
Then he'd target the former minister directly.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.370
That's true...

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:46.250
<b>Professor: The real destruction is yet to come.</b>

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.900
"The real destruction is yet to come."

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.670
In the scenario that Director 
Kadoyama wrote himself,

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:54.530
a biologist looks at the destroyed 
city hall and says this:

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.180
"The real destruction is yet to come.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:00.280
A destruction sufficient to crush a great city."

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.630
And three days later, 
this is what the scenario says.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.060
"Commander! Rudra appeared again!"

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:07.860
Where?

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:08.650
Where?

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.610
The data in the scenario ends there.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:14.320
It ends?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.530
<b>Soldier: Commander! 

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.530
It seems he kept the climax 
in another, top-secret file.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:22.820
If his real revenge is just about to begin...

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.350
Bad news, everyone.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.830
What is it, Funasaka-san?

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:32.720
We've found where the explosives 
at the old city hall came from.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.200
The brand name is "Image Master."

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.840
Those got into Japan?!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.480
I'm told the mafia smuggled them in

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.890
and hid them in an abandoned building 
in the quicksand district.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.550
So they were stolen?

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.300
Yes, last month.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.440
And the real problem is the amount.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:52.290
The last explosion used 0.2 tons.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.820
But 400 tons were stolen!

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:56.770
Two thousand times the last one?

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:58.990
If they were all used...

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.140
Tokyo would be annihilated.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:05.490
Let's go talk to the film crew!

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.130
There might be a hint to the next location!

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:07.770
Impossible.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:08.460
Why?

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:12.130
If this follows the scenario, the real 
explosion takes place in two days.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:16.640
We can't reach the staff scattered 
around the world that quickly.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.360
Assuming he's out for revenge,

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.610
we can check places associated 
with Mouri Takerou,

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.510
like his hometown or election district.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.250
Nagoya!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:30.230
He said he was going home 
to prepare for the next election.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.410
Asami-chan is already in Nagoya,

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.890
looking for projectors and explosives.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.030
If she finds anything, she'll call us at once.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.740
<b>Kazari Asami</b>

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:41.150
This is Unit 9, Oscar VI.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:41.740
That was fast!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.440
I've engaged an unidentified 
Willwear in combat.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.830
There really was someone behind this!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.820
Oscar VI, can you send video?

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:49.790
I'll try.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.850
That's the one from the suicide bombing!

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:56.440
What is that? It's disgusting!

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:59.010
The person inside is way too flexible.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:01.000
Be careful, Oscar VI!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.290
He's tough!

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:03.350
No problem.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:04.470
Fingers!

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:05.790
Yes, Brain!

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:07.400
You're under arrest!

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.580
You're under arrest!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.940
Judgment of Justice!

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:18.030
Perfect Charge: Digamma!

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:25.110
Didn't she just hit her own subordinates, too?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.340
Poor guys.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.660
Kyoukai-kun, are you there?

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:30.620
What is it, Kyoukai-sama?

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:34.710
Something about the Willwear was 
bothering me, so I looked into it.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:36.590
And I was right.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.640
A robot?

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:40.590
That explains it!

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.280
I think this

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:45.720
might have been developed 
by the Carupanuba Junta.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:46.740
Yes...

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.150
It's entered the production stage, hasn't it?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.340
Kyoukai-sama!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.070
Don't worry.

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:56.510
All our members are safe.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:04.030
And we also found a trailer that contained 
a fog machine and 3-D projectors.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:06.870
But it caught fire and burned 
before we could secure it.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.670
They covered up the evidence?

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:09.580
Probably.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.560
Great, what do we do now?

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.080
I'll leave you to decide.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:14.970
Roger.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.410
We'll have them keep 
searching Aichi Prefecture.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.380
For now, Sena-kun...

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:22.200
Yes?

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.350
Tell me where to find the best 
restaurants in Nagoya!

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:25.990
Huh?

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:27.230
Because...

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:30.140
We're almost at Nagoya.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.940
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.150
Eat this so you can work 
your a**es off tomorrow,

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.660
you scumwad d**ks!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.300
Thank you, ma'am!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.800
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.370
I asked her, and she said 
to have you eat here.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.750
But you have both doteni and Ise udon.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.830
That's plenty.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.040
I wish Unit 9 could have joined us...

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.330
Even if it was to solve the case,

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.390
they let everything get way out of hand.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:04.630
More letters of apology?

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:09.390
Still, it's just like you to prioritize 
the hiring of immigrants.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.620
No, that's not what I'm doing at all.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.770
You're so humble!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:17.000
Stop sitting around, CEO B*nerface!

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.540
Yes, ma'am!

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.140
Scumbags!

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.440
Gl*ry h*le!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:27.290
But I'm glad we managed to stop Rudra 
from causing problems here.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:31.100
It's rare for you to be so attached to something.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.000
I may be the person I am

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.500
because of Kadoyama-san.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.420
What happened?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.810
Right after I joined the force,

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.920
I was in Division 5's anti-gang task force.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.090
What, you're proud of that?

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.090
I went after the son of a certain 
powerful figure too hard,

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.990
so they pulled strings to get me transferred.

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:54.060
I was sent to Unit 8.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.770
Yeah, I heard the stories.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.980
I'm sorry to say this, 
but I was sulking over that.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.300
And then,

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:05.940
I happened to visit Kadoyama-san's 
studio during an investigation.

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:11.570
Oh, you're the detective who's 
here over the drug case?

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.040
I'm sorry.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:17.000
We're aware this place has nothing to do 
with the case, but I must be sure.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:22.960
<b>Fragile 

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.590
It's fine.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.960
These buildings are so well-made, though.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.170
And this, too.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.390
Do you know what they're made from?

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:29.680
Plaster or something?

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:34.230
They're actually wafers from a 
place called Altea, in Setogaya.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:35.930
Wafers?

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.140
Yes, the candy.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:40.270
We tried many different things,

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.460
and these break the best.

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.400
Oh...

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:46.540
Are you disappointed that we use 
something so old-fashioned?

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:47.360
Oh, no.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.600
Director, the set's finished.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.270
Watch if you like.

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:52.270
Okay.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.540
<b>Kadoyama Team</b>

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:54.540
Ready... Action!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.370
Rolling!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.040
And cut!

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:05.690
Cut!

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.110
Cut!

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:07.170
Douse the fires!

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.320
I was amazed at how much punch it had.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.140
They tell me that these days, it's old-fashioned.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.510
Then, why?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.640
I went to see a movie by one 
of the younger generation.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.530
The kids there seemed strangely disinterested.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.840
The CG people had worked really hard,

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.310
but the kids didn't care.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:32.200
So I asked if they didn't like it.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.650
And one of the kids said that it looked cheap.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:39.210
I thought they'd worked hard,

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:42.800
but even if I cared, the customers didn't.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:43.950
Yes...

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:46.100
You can't just try to satisfy yourself.

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:48.710
So I made my decision.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.800
If I don't have any money,

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:55.690
I'd rather use old-fashioned special 
effects than some lousy CG.

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:56.680
I understand.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.070
The old ways have their own advantages.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:02.860
I believe that if you don't cut corners, 
the audience can tell how you feel.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.790
How you feel?

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.980
If you sulk, you lose.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.450
The world's full of things that aren't fair.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.910
But that doesn't mean you can 
shut down, or that it's over for you.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.860
I'll be 74 this year,

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:21.660
and I want to make a movie that combines 
CG and old-fashioned special effects.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.290
Please do. Make something amazing.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.290
I will! Something that'll amaze everyone!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:35.050
That's what helped me get over everything 
and accept the transfer to Section 8.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.870
You quit in the end, though.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.140
That's all right because I'm 
satisfied with my life.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.140
Now, now...

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:42.780
So I owe Kadoyama-san a lot.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.630
Why would such a good person do this?

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:45.350
No.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:50.280
I think someone is using him.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.270
If you sulk, you lose.

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:55.160
If you stop just because things 
aren't fair, it's all over, he said.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:56.740
He wouldn't...

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.440
I want to apprehend whoever is 
doing this, and learn the truth.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.460
So that I can keep believing in 
the man who kept me going.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.340
Thanks.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:10.670
No explosives were found in 
Minister Mouri's hometown.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.910
Then Nagoya wasn't the target?

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.470
There is a chance you're right.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:19.350
I found a video taken before 
Director Kadoyama's death.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.360
<i>Skyscrapers these days</i>

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.510
<i>don't really work with giant monsters.</i>

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.310
<i>They're too tall.</i>

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.510
Would someone like that

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:31.660
choose the area in front of Nagoya 
Station for a giant monster attack?

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:37.030
It's true, you wouldn't be able 
to see the monster at all.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.970
So I looked into it,

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:41.410
and Minister Mouri was born in Nagoya,

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.380
but grew up mostly in Bunkyou Ward.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.650
He only ran from Nagoya for 
internal political reasons.

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:49.250
Isn't Bunkyou Ward...

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:52.040
Yes, a priority redevelopment area.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.920
Many small-story buildings in that area

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.970
are perfect for a monster attack.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.930
So this was a decoy?

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:01.260
We're heading back to Tokyo.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:02.980
Everyone, get ready!

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:03.950
Right!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.190
They found explosives in the ward.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:13.130
But only some of them.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:16.970
The evacuation's complete in 
a one-kilometer radius.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:19.200
<b>Let's Bring in the Showa Special Ward 

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.630
If Image Master bombs are used,

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.580
<b>Governor Inagi Must Resign!!</b>

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.580
we'll need more than that.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.990
Someone has to get there first... and...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.700
Kuroki-kun!

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.000
He can't go. That would be drunk Willwearing.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:32.090
He was drinking at a fast pace...

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:36.170
If they're following the scenario, 
Rudra will appear at midnight.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.280
Kyoukai-san, any options for us?

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.220
If we fill the sky with chaff, we might 
be able to stop the detonation.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.110
But where can we get all that chaff?

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:46.350
The Unified SDF should keep a stock

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.560
at the Fuchuuhon-machi factory.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.440
The Unified SDF...

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.400
He blew off our meeting two 
and a half months ago!

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.440
Yes.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.240
I understand how you feel.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:01.570
He answers my messages at a 4.3% rate.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.020
I am very sorry.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.320
He went to Nagoya without even telling me.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:09.570
And if he hates the USDF so much, he shouldn't be asking for help!

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:12.330
You are absolutely right, yes.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:16.550
But we need your help to protect 
the lives of our citizens!

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:18.990
I understand.

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:20.390
Thank you!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:23.610
Funasaka-san, could you give a 
message to Souichirou for me?

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.750
Ah, of course.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:27.270
Tell him this will cost him.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.730
Rudra has appeared in Bunkyou Ward.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:48.700
Where's Oscar I?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:54.170
<b>Nagoya</b>

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.470
Maintaining planned altitude and speed.

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:52.420
Roger.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.170
Let's get ready, too.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.560
<i>I won't let you</i>

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:01.550
<i>use Kadoyama-san's Rudra for this anymore.</i>

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:03.550
Ultra-long-range sniper rifle

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.960
Shiden Seisou Custom ready to launch!

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:07.100
Launch!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.140
Souichirou,

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.660
I look forward to your thanking me.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:14.940
There it is.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.990
Oscar I, I'm sending data on the firing point.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.990
The flight structure is unstable,

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:24.990
so be careful when you use it.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:25.870
Roger!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.800
We're above Bunkyou Ward.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.630
The monster has appeared again.

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:36.610
Police say that evacuation is complete.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:41.100
It's firing its beam!

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:41.880
Oscar I!

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:42.760
Kadoyama-san...

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.480
Rudra has fired its beam!

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:54.190
The city has turned into a sea of flame!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.980
Or... it hasn't?

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.570
It's Unit 8!

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.240
Unit 8 did it!

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:05.240
Our sources tell us they've deployed

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:08.550
a jamming material, which stopped 
the remote detonation.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.640
Which means...

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.880
My broadcast cut out?

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.920
If that's the case, I'm sorry, everyone!

00:21:19.350 --> 00:21:23.240
I'm glad Rudra didn't have to destroy the city.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:26.400
Kadoyama-san, everyone will 
know how you felt—

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.160
You!

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.200
H-How?

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:42.390
Wired detonators?

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:43.260
Yeah.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.320
We discovered them from the recovered 
explosives and Willwear.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:47.530
I see.

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:51.820
And at the police conference
today, it was decided that

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.470
your savior, Kadoyama-san, wasn't involved.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.330
They said his footage was probably just used.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:02.000
Jirou says there's a chance he's involved.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.050
Hachijou?

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.110
Yeah.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:09.060
He probably used Kadoyama-san's 
work for his games.

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:09.930
Games?

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:13.060
Then I will never forgive him!

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:15.640
I will catch him!

00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:20.140
I never thought

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:23.150
I'd be able to play a game in this country.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.370
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:56.820
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:55.620 --> 00:24:09.040
File 7: Absolute Peeping Declaration

00:23:56.820 --> 00:23:58.300
What's that, Souichirou?

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.580
Miho, you're not supposed 
to be in the next episode.

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:01.440
That's right!

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:04.820
It's the swimsuit episode, and I'm not in it?!

00:24:04.820 --> 00:24:08.160
But I'll watch over you, even if I have to leave 
my body and do it from the spirit world.
